  "setting": "Alternate Cold War: a Soviet-organised South Slav state that includes Bulgaria, and a Warsaw Pact member. Its real domestic arms industry survives (M-84, M-80A, M-60P, BOV, M-77 Oganj) alongside Soviet exports. Troops run the gamut: mostly decent, with poor and good pockets; the Proleterska Garda is the only formation that is consistently good.",
  "scale_note": "1:5 formations are the source of truth, in the style of the rulebook's Appendix E army lists (Rule 2.2: one vehicle stand = 4-6 vehicles, one infantry stand = a platoon). Each battalion type also has a 1:1 breakdown per Chapter 26 (one stand = one vehicle or one infantry squad; organise stands into companies). Equipment Notes name catalog cards valid for each year band; an entry with only_for replaces the general entry for those quality groups in overlapping years. Roles listed under roles_without_cards have no catalog card yet (infantry, artillery, trucks, engineers). Validate edits with: npm run check:toe",
